course: dictionary
lesson: 6940
title: Painful: hurting, upsetting or very slow
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Painful» is an adjective, so it describes a noun. It has three meanings. The first is about the body: a painful knee or a painful bee sting hurts. The second is about feelings: a painful memory or a painful goodbye makes you sad or upset. The third is about something very hard or slow to watch or do.
explain: Use the clues around the word to choose the right meaning. «A boy in California sat on a fire ant nest; hundreds of ants stung him, and he had painful blisters for days.» Blisters hurt, so painful means causing pain here. «Bending down can be hard or painful for older people.» Hard and painful sit together, so it means difficult to do without hurting.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If "causing pain" or "hurting" fits, you have the body meaning. If "sad" or "upset" fits better, you have the feelings meaning. If "so slow it is hard to watch" fits, you have the third meaning.
fact: Painful means causing pain or hurting, as in «a painful knee».
fact: Painful can mean making you feel sad, upset or embarrassed, as in «a painful memory».
fact: Painful can also mean very hard or slow to watch or do, as in «painfully slow».
fact: «The bullet ant has one of the most painful insect stings known, and the pain can last for many hours.» Here painful means causing very strong pain.
fact: Painful is an adjective, and it changes for comparing: painful, more painful, most painful.
exercise: «A boy in California had painful blisters for days.» What does painful mean here? | *Causing pain or hurting | Making him feel embarrassed in front of friends | Very slow to heal, like a snail | Bright red in colour
exercise: Mia says the bus queue was painfully slow. What does painfully slow mean? | Very fast and exciting | *So slow that it is hard to watch or bear | Slow, but gentle and kind | Quiet, like a whisper
exercise: Which phrase uses painful to mean making you feel sad or upset? | painful to hold | a painful knee | *a painful memory | a painful bee sting
test: «The bullet ant has one of the most painful insect stings known.» What does most painful tell you? | *It causes more pain than the other stings in the group | It makes people laugh | It causes the least pain of all the stings | It does not hurt at all
test: What does painful mean in «a painful goodbye»? | Very fast and loud | Full of pain from a hurt body | Warm and cosy | *Upsetting and sad
exam: Which sentence uses painful to mean very hard or slow to watch? | The bee sting was painful | His painful knee needed ice | She had a painful memory of the flood | *The match was painfully slow, with no goals for an hour
